From 5a89b1adcab5d4295fd20c5c3e29b717cfcf11ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naruto Recomp <local@invalid>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 18:51:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] feat(audio): add per-stream continuity and output flow
 telemetry

Cutscene audio defects have never been captured with instrumentation, which is
why several audio scenarios have stayed pending. Add the measurement first.

Per XMA context, accumulate decoded frames, buffer swaps, loop rewinds, decode
errors and decodes that restart from an offset already covered since the last
swap. Decoded audio seconds over real seconds gives a fill ratio: a healthy
stream reports 1.0, a starving one reports less, and a stream repeating a
section stays near 1.0 while offset repeats climb, which separates repetition
from starvation without guessing.

On the output side, count queue depth, starved chunks and waveform
discontinuities at buffer seams, measured before concealment smooths them.

All counters are incremented under locks the audio paths already hold, and all
formatting happens on the decoder or audio worker thread. Nothing is added to
the real-time callback, because periodic I/O there was already identified as a
source of dropouts and removed once.

Both reports are disabled by default.
